.SH NAME
frontend/node_modules/readdirp Directory Reference
.SH SYNOPSIS
.br
.PP
.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 

.SH "readdirp [![Weekly downloads](https://img.shields.io/npm/dw/readdirp.svg)](https://github.com/paulmillr/readdirp)"
.PP
Recursive version of \fRfs\&.readdir\fP\&. Exposes a \fBstream API\fP and a \fBpromise API\fP\&.

.PP
.PP
.nf
npm install readdirp
.fi
.PP

.PP
.PP
.nf
const readdirp = require('readdirp');

// Use streams to achieve small RAM & CPU footprint\&.
// 1) Streams example with for\-await\&.
for await (const entry of readdirp('\&.')) {
  const {path} = entry;
  console\&.log(`${JSON\&.stringify({path})}`);
}

// 2) Streams example, non for\-await\&.
// Print out all JS files along with their size within the current folder & subfolders\&.
readdirp('\&.', {fileFilter: '*\&.js', alwaysStat: true})
  \&.on('data', (entry) => {
    const {path, stats: {size}} = entry;
    console\&.log(`${JSON\&.stringify({path, size})}`);
  })
  // Optionally call stream\&.destroy() in `warn()` in order to abort and cause 'close' to be emitted
  \&.on('warn', error => console\&.error('non\-fatal error', error))
  \&.on('error', error => console\&.error('fatal error', error))
  \&.on('end', () => console\&.log('done'));

// 3) Promise example\&. More RAM and CPU than streams / for\-await\&.
const files = await readdirp\&.promise('\&.');
console\&.log(files\&.map(file => file\&.path));

// Other options\&.
readdirp('test', {
  fileFilter: '*\&.js',
  directoryFilter: ['!\&.git', '!*modules']
  // directoryFilter: (di) => di\&.basename\&.length === 9
  type: 'files_directories',
  depth: 1
});
.fi
.PP

.PP
For more examples, check out \fRexamples\fP directory\&.
.SH "API"
.PP
\fRconst stream = readdirp(root[, options])\fP — \fBStream API\fP

.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
Reads given root recursively and returns a \fRstream\fP of \fBentry infos\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
Optionally can be used like \fRfor await (const entry of stream)\fP with node\&.js 10+ (\fRasyncIterator\fP)\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRon('data', (entry) => {})\fP \fBentry info\fP for every file / dir\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRon('warn', (error) => {})\fP non-fatal \fRError\fP that prevents a file / dir from being processed\&. Example: inaccessible to the user\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRon('error', (error) => {})\fP fatal \fRError\fP which also ends the stream\&. Example: illegal options where passed\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRon('end')\fP — we are done\&. Called when all entries were found and no more will be emitted\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRon('close')\fP — stream is destroyed via \fRstream\&.destroy()\fP\&. Could be useful if you want to manually abort even on a non fatal error\&. At that point the stream is no longer \fRreadable\fP and no more entries, warning or errors are emitted
.IP "\(bu" 2
To learn more about streams, consult the very detailed \fRnodejs streams documentation\fP or the \fRstream-handbook\fP
.PP

.PP
\fRconst entries = await readdirp\&.promise(root[, options])\fP — \fBPromise API\fP\&. Returns a list of \fBentry infos\fP\&.

.PP
First argument is awalys \fRroot\fP, path in which to start reading and recursing into subdirectories\&.
.SS "options"
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRfileFilter: ["*\&.js"]\fP: filter to include or exclude files\&. A \fRFunction\fP, Glob string or Array of glob strings\&.
.IP "  \(bu" 4
\fBFunction\fP: a function that takes an entry info as a parameter and returns true to include or false to exclude the entry
.IP "  \(bu" 4
\fBGlob string\fP: a string (e\&.g\&., \fR*\&.js\fP) which is matched using \fRpicomatch\fP, so go there for more information\&. Globstars (\fR**\fP) are not supported since specifying a recursive pattern for an already recursive function doesn't make sense\&. Negated globs (as explained in the minimatch documentation) are allowed, e\&.g\&., \fR!*\&.txt\fP matches everything but text files\&.
.IP "  \(bu" 4
\fBArray of glob strings\fP: either need to be all inclusive or all exclusive (negated) patterns otherwise an error is thrown\&. \fR['*\&.json', '*\&.js']\fP includes all JavaScript and Json files\&. \fR['!\&.git', '!node_modules']\fP includes all directories except the '\&.git' and 'node_modules'\&.
.IP "  \(bu" 4
Directories that do not pass a filter will not be recursed into\&.
.PP

.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRdirectoryFilter: ['!\&.git']\fP: filter to include/exclude directories found and to recurse into\&. Directories that do not pass a filter will not be recursed into\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRdepth: 5\fP: depth at which to stop recursing even if more subdirectories are found
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRtype: 'files'\fP: determines if data events on the stream should be emitted for \fR'files'\fP (default), \fR'directories'\fP, \fR'files_directories'\fP, or \fR'all'\fP\&. Setting to \fR'all'\fP will also include entries for other types of file descriptors like character devices, unix sockets and named pipes\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRalwaysStat: false\fP: always return \fRstats\fP property for every file\&. Default is \fRfalse\fP, readdirp will return \fRDirent\fP entries\&. Setting it to \fRtrue\fP can double readdir execution time - use it only when you need file \fRsize\fP, \fRmtime\fP etc\&. Cannot be enabled on node <10\&.10\&.0\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRlstat: false\fP: include symlink entries in the stream along with files\&. When \fRtrue\fP, \fRfs\&.lstat\fP would be used instead of \fRfs\&.stat\fP
.PP
.SS "\fREntryInfo\fP"
Has the following properties:

.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRpath: 'assets/javascripts/react\&.js'\fP: path to the file/directory (relative to given root)
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRfullPath: '/Users/dev/projects/app/assets/javascripts/react\&.js'\fP: full path to the file/directory found
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRbasename: 'react\&.js'\fP: name of the file/directory
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRdirent: fs\&.Dirent\fP: built-in \fRdir entry object\fP - only with \fRalwaysStat: false\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRstats: fs\&.Stats\fP: built in \fRstat object\fP - only with \fRalwaysStat: true\fP
.PP
.SH "Changelog"
.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
3\&.5 (Oct 13, 2020) disallows recursive directory-based symlinks\&. Before, it could have entered infinite loop\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
3\&.4 (Mar 19, 2020) adds support for directory-based symlinks\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
3\&.3 (Dec 6, 2019) stabilizes RAM consumption and enables perf management with \fRhighWaterMark\fP option\&. Fixes race conditions related to \fRfor-await\fP looping\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
3\&.2 (Oct 14, 2019) improves performance by 250% and makes streams implementation more idiomatic\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
3\&.1 (Jul 7, 2019) brings \fRbigint\fP support to \fRstat\fP output on Windows\&. This is backwards-incompatible for some cases\&. Be careful\&. It you use it incorrectly, you'll see "TypeError: Cannot mix BigInt and other types, use explicit conversions"\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
3\&.0 brings huge performance improvements and stream backpressure support\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
Upgrading 2\&.x to 3\&.x:
.IP "  \(bu" 4
Signature changed from \fRreaddirp(options)\fP to \fRreaddirp(root, options)\fP
.IP "  \(bu" 4
Replaced callback API with promise API\&.
.IP "  \(bu" 4
Renamed \fRentryType\fP option to \fRtype\fP
.IP "  \(bu" 4
Renamed \fRentryType: 'both'\fP to \fR'files_directories'\fP
.IP "  \(bu" 4
\fREntryInfo\fP
.IP "    \(bu" 6
Renamed \fRstat\fP to \fRstats\fP
.IP "      \(bu" 8
Emitted only when \fRalwaysStat: true\fP
.IP "      \(bu" 8
\fRdirent\fP is emitted instead of \fRstats\fP by default with \fRalwaysStat: false\fP
.PP

.IP "    \(bu" 6
Renamed \fRname\fP to \fRbasename\fP
.IP "    \(bu" 6
Removed \fRparentDir\fP and \fRfullParentDir\fP properties
.PP

.PP

.IP "\(bu" 2
Supported node\&.js versions:
.IP "  \(bu" 4
3\&.x: node 8+
.IP "  \(bu" 4
2\&.x: node 0\&.6+
.PP

